1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[narrator] Heavens Arena.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
The 251-story building

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
which stands 991 meters tall

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
is a mecca for fighters.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
When combatants win a fight,

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
they may advance by one class,

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
and receive a corresponding reward.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
After reaching the 100th floor,
they are assigned a private room.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
And those contestants
who are skilled and fortunate enough

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
to reach the 200th floor,

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
earn the right to challenge
the strongest fighters, the Floor Masters,

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
in an intense battle for survival.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
This is, without a doubt,

14
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
the best stage a warrior could ask for.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[theme song playing]

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[Sadaso]
Today, I’ll beat Killua for my sixth win.

17
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Tomorrow, I'll beat Gon
for my seventh win.

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
After that

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
all I’ll need to do
is find three more suckers...

20
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
[chuckling]

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
...then I’ll be a Floor Master!

22
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
With the kind of fame and fortune
that’ll get me,

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
I’ll be set for the rest of my life!

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
[gasps]

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Killua] You move, you die.

26
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You use Nen and you die.

27
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Make a sound and you die.

28
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
If you understand, close your eyes.

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Do you see what happens
when you break your promises?

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
If you do, open your eyes,

31
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
look at me in the mirror
and listen carefully.

32
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Don’t ever show your dirty face
in front of us again.

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
You’ll keep this promise.

34
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,000
POWER x TO x AVENGE

35
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
[narrator] There are many who would resort
to using underhanded tactics

36
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
to become a Floor Master.

37
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Gon, on the other hand,

38
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
has been fiercely concentrating

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
on improving his Nen
and growing stronger.

40
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
And tonight,
he has his battle with Sadaso.

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
[Sadaso] His eyes…

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
they belong to someone
who lives in the world of darkness.

43
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
I was filled with despair.

44
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
I could sense the difference in strength
the second our eyes met.

45
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
It was clear that he was the predator
and I was his prey.

46
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
It was a huge mistake
to underestimate him.

47
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
He isn’t just some normal kid.

48
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
I don’t want to die,

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
so I’m getting the hell out of here.

50
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
You should be careful.

51
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
He’ll be coming after you guys next!

52
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[disconnected call signal]

53
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
[Gido] Now what?

54
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Well, I’m still in.

55
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
And I’m willing to do whatever it takes.

56
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
I’m almost a Floor Master.

57
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Ten victories on this floor

58
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
and you’re allowed
to challenge a Floor Master.

59
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,000
If you win,
you get an entire floor to yourself.

60
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[uneasy grunting]

61
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
And as soon as that title is in your hand,

62
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
you can lecture, teach, and advise.

63
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Or start up a martial arts school.

64
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
For the rest of your life,

65
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
you’ve got it made.

66
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
[Gido] Do you think that kid’s
gonna come back here to threaten us?

67
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
[Riehlvelt]
The boy has no clue what my abilities are.

68
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
As long as we’re careful about it,

69
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
we should be able
to handle him quite easily.

70
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
-[Killua] You're wrong.
-[Riehlvelt and Gido gasp]

71
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
It doesn’t really matter
what your abilities are.

72
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[Gido groans]

73
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
There’s no rush.

74
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
You see… I can always get to you.

75
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Whenever and wherever I want.

76
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
At night, when you’re sound asleep
in your bed...

77
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
when you’re taking a crap…

78
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Right?

79
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Listen up.

80
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
You should follow the rules.

81
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Without the rules,

82
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
the only ones benefitting would be us.

83
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
[chuckles]

84
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
As I was saying:
cheating is a terrible idea.

85
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
A fair fight is the way to go.

86
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Right.

87
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
[referee] Sadaso’s time is up!

88
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Gon wins by default!

89
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
[spectator 1] What? Again?

90
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[spectator 2]
Yeah, what the hell is Sadaso doing?

91
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:26,000
JUNE 1

92
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:32,000
JUNE 2

93
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:38,000
JUNE 3

94
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
JUNE 4

95
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
[Wing] All right. So today…

96
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Gon will be fighting Gido.

97
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
After that, of course,

98
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Killua will be going up against Riehlvelt.

99
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Are you both feeling all right?

100
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[both] Yes sir.

101
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Now, this will be your second match
against Gido,

102
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
so I doubt you’ll require much advice.

103
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Have you settled on a strategy?

104
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Yes.

105
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
I, uh... think I have.
Well, here’s the thing…

106
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
My strategy is to use that.

107
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
[Killua] Huh?

108
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Yes, I understand.

109
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[cheering]

110
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Cocco] The rematch
you’ve all been waiting for

111
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
is finally here!

112
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Gido versus Gon!

113
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Their last match landed Gon
in the hospital

114
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
but there’s no telling
what we’re in for this time!

115
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
For today’s match,
Gon is carrying a fishing rod!

116
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
But how exactly does he plan to use it?

117
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Will he be incorporating it
into his fighting style?

118
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Let’s find out!

119
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
This is a points and KO system.

120
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
No time limit!

121
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Begin!

122
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
[Cocco] Right off the bat,
Gon takes off in a mad dash!

123
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
But it looks like Gido
was prepared for this!

124
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
He’s already responding
with his Tornado Top!

125
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
If Gon charges in,

126
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
he’ll be in the same position
he was last time!

127
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Gon] He’s way ahead of me.

128
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[Gido cackling]

129
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
[Gido] I know what you’re thinking.

130
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Once I’ve started spinning,

131
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
it’s virtually impossible to stop me!

132
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,000
The only logical course would be to hit me

133
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
with a preemptive attack
before I even start.

134
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Well, if you’re not going to make a move,
I will!

135
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Shotgun Blues!

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
SHOTGUN BLUES

137
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
He can fire off his tops mid-spin?

138
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[Gido] As you can see,

139
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
this technique
is nothing like the Battle Waltz!

140
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
All my tops will be aiming right for you!

141
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
You’ll never be able to dodge them all!

142
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Ren!

143
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[Gido] What?!

144
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
-[audience] Ooh!
-Whoa! He stopped them!

145
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Did you just see that?

146
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Oh, wow…

147
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
[Cocco] That was incredible!

148
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Gon just blocked the tops head-on!

149
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
He is not the same competitor
he was two months ago!

150
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
[Gido] Argh! Damn!

151
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
His Nen defenses have shot way up!

152
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Will my tops still be enough to beat him?

153
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
[Killua]
Those tops were coming straight at him.

154
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
With his reflexes,

155
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Gon could’ve knocked them all down
with his fishing rod.

156
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
But he chose to go with Ren instead…

157
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
and that did way
more psychological damage to Gido.

158
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
He must be thinking about
how they used Zushi to blackmail us...

159
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
and he’s furious.

160
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Okay, it’s my turn now!

161
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
[Cocco] I wonder what technique
Gon will use this time, folks!

162
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[Gido] He’s using a fishing rod

163
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
and that can only mean one thing…

164
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:51,000
he’ll try to snag my clothes
and bring my spinning to a halt!

165
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
But it’s not going to be that easy.

166
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[grunts]

167
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[Cocco] There it is!
He’s going straight for Gido!

168
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
[cackling] I knew it.

169
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Not gonna happen!

170
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[Cocco] Oh, no!

171
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
His attack missed its target!

172
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[Gido]
[cackling] What were you even aiming at?

173
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[roaring]

174
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
What the--?!

175
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Cocco] Unbelievable!

176
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Gon flipped the floor tile
and Gido along with it!

177
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
[screaming]

178
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[groaning]

179
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
[yells]

180
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[grunts]

181
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
-[roaring]
-No! Wait!

182
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[Cocco] G-- Gon has just broken
Gido’s steel prosthetic leg,

183
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
making it very unlikely
that he’ll be able to continue the fight!

184
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
[Gon] If you guys resort to any means,

185
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
then we won’t hold back, either!

186
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
And if you even touch Zushi ever again,

187
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
next time I see you,
I’ll break your face in half!

188
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
[moaning]

189
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
[referee] The winner is... Gon!

190
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[cheering]

191
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Cocco] Gon was finally able
to avenge his initial loss to Gido!

192
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:35,000
His record on the 200th floor
is now two to one!

193
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
All right. Guess I’m up next.

194
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[Cocco]
And now for the main event of the day…

195
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Killua versus Riehlvelt!

196
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Since Sadaso forfeited the previous match,

197
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:00,000
this will technically be Killua’s
200th floor debut!

198
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
What kind of strategy
are we about to see now?

199
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
You do realize
that you broke your promise first.

200
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
There’s no way I’ll let you win now.

201
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
[Sadaso] His eyes…

202
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
they belong to someone
who lives in the world of darkness.

203
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
[Riehlvelt] “Someone who lives
in the world of darkness”?

204
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,000
So, what if this brat
is a professional assassin?

205
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Heavens Arena is my turf!

206
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
It’s time for me to show him

207
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
that within the four sides
of this square stage…

208
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
I rule!

209
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Go, Killua! You can do it!

210
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
This is a points and KO system!

211
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
No time limit!

212
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Begin!

213
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
He vanished?

214
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Behind me!

215
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Aura Burst!

216
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
AURA BURST

217
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[Cocco]
Riehlvelt boosted out of harm’s way!

218
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,000
He propels his wheelchair
by releasing his stored aura,

219
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
guiding it to wherever he wants to go!

220
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
I jumped too high.

221
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Whew. That was close.

222
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Two Headed Snake: Twin Serpents!

223
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Song of Defense!

224
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
SONG OF DEFENSE

225
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
[Cocco] There it is, folks!

226
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Riehlvelt’s Song of Defense!

227
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
He protects himself with two whips,

228
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,000
moving at ridiculously high speeds

229
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
then waits patiently
for his chance to strike!

230
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Riehlvelt] You planned to attack first
and take the lead.

231
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Too bad that didn’t work for ya!

232
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Now that I’ve taken this stance,

233
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
there is no way you could possibly win!

234
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Why’s that?

235
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
[Riehlvelt] It’s obvious, isn’t it?

236
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
No normal person on the planet
can keep up with these two whips!

237
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
And on this little platform,
there’s nowhere you can run and hide!

238
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
[sighs]

239
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Take this!

240
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Yeah? Well, I’m not normal.

241
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Sorry ‘bout that.

242
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[Riehlvelt] What?!

243
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Fine, then.

244
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Thunder Serpent!

245
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[Killua straining]

246
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Hmm...

247
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
I’m surprised, Killua!

248
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
You’re the first person I’ve fought
who could see my whips in motion!

249
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
So, I’ve got a little present for you!

250
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Those two whips together
carry one million volts!

251
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:21,000
More than enough
to paralyze and incapacitate a giant!

252
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Anyone foolish enough to resist my whips,

253
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
will fall victim
to the mighty Thunder Serpent!

254
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
[Riehlvelt shrieking]

255
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
I’m trained to endure torture,

256
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
so electricity won’t work.

257
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
It has no effect on me.

258
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
I mean, I can tolerate it...

259
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
But it isn’t like it makes me happy.

260
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
It still really hurts a lot
and everything.

261
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
That's why I'm a little pissed.

262
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
[crazed chuckle]

263
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[Killua] There’s no way you can survive
a fall from that height.

264
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
So, what do you wanna do?

265
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Riehlvelt]
Catch me! Please! Don’t let me die!

266
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Okay then.

267
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Don’t worry; I’m right here for you!

268
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[frightened cry]

269
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[high-pitched scream of pain]

270
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
[crazed chuckle]

271
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
[shuddering breath]

272
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Damn it.

273
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
At least now you know
how much that hurts, you idiot.

274
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Riehlvelt is down
and so, by virtue of a knockdown,

275
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Killua takes the victory!

276
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
[cheering]

277
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[Zushi shouting and laughing]

278
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Nice job, Killua!

279
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
[Killua chuckles]

280
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Thanks!

281
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
That means you’re up next.

282
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,000
How long ‘til you fight him? Ten days?

283
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Yup. It’ll be on June 10th.

284
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Just remember what worked for me
isn’t gonna work for you, okay?

285
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
If those electric whips
so much as touch you,

286
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
you’ll be out cold
before you even know what’s happening.

287
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Mm-hmm.

288
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
What’s your strategy?

289
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Oh, don’t worry. I think I have an idea.

290
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Oh?

291
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
You weren’t watching for nothing, were ya?

292
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Guess you prefer combat to observing, too.

293
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Hmm...

294
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
[chuckles quietly]

295
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,000
JUNE 9

296
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
[Cocco] It appears that the damage
Gido sustained in his match with Gon

297
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
was so severe

298
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
that he hasn’t returned for today’s fight.

299
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[referee]
The winner by default is… Killua!

300
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
JUNE 10

301
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
[Cocco] After losing to Killua,
Riehlvelt’s record is five-three.

302
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
He can’t afford another loss!

303
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
As you know, after four losses
you’re out of the contest

304
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
and have to start over from square one!

305
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
He must be wary of Gon’s speed,

306
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
because he’s got his whips out already.

307
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Meanwhile, Gon isn’t carrying
his fishing rod.

308
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:23,000
He’s completely empty-handed!

309
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
How does he plan to fight this time?

310
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Begin!

311
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:31,000
[Cocco]
Song of Defense, right from the start!

312
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Riehlvelt wants to end this fight
in a hurry!

313
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Hmm...

314
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[Cocco] What’s this? Gon is… squatting?

315
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
[roaring]

316
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[Cocco] He just ripped up the stone tile
with his bare hands, folks!

317
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
-[roars]
-[Cocco] And now he threw it!

318
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
[Riehlvelt] Aura Burst!

319
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Cocco] He escaped in the nick of time!

320
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[Killua]
He left him a way out on purpose….

321
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Riehlvelt gasps in shock]

322
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[Cocco] But Gon anticipated that move,

323
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
and he’s already one step ahead!

324
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[Hisoka]
When you’re trying to escape,

325
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
every fraction of a second counts.

326
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
And without time to change direction,

327
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
all you can do is continue
to move forward.

328
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,000
And accelerating as quickly as that
will throw you off-balance.

329
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
His only option at that point
was to stop the whips.

330
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
That’s the time to move in!

331
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
[screaming in pain]

332
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,000
[wheezing]

333
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
So, this is the switch, huh?

334
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Let’s see…

335
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
I’ll just turn it up to the max.

336
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
No! Stop!

337
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Switch it…

338
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Stop it!

339
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
...on!

340
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Just kidding.

341
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Riehlvelt is down!

342
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
That counts as a knockout.

343
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
The win goes to Gon!

344
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
[cheering]

345
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Hey, Gon!

346
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[clapping]

347
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Splendid. Just splendid.

348
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Including your last two matches,

349
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
you’ve made progress.

350
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
You've made the grade,

351
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,000
so set the time and place
of your choosing.

352
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
I’ll take you on any time.

353
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
[determined grunt]

354
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
[narrator] The strength that Gon
demonstrated in his matches

355
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
did not escape Hisoka unnoticed.

356
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
It won’t be long now
before their fight begins.

357
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[theme song playing]

358
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[Gon] Coming up:

359
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

360
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

361
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

362
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

363
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Today, we're introducing Cocco.

364
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,000
She announces all of the fights
at Heavens Arena!

365
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Oh. You mean the lady
who’s always talking, huh?

366
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
I wonder… how many of her are there?

367
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
You think there are mor--?!

368
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
[Gon] Next time: “The x True x Pass”!

369
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Killua.

370
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
What does ‘so-and-so
and such-and-such’ mean?

371
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Killua] You really don’t know?

372
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
It means "so and so and such and such"!
